# Build context is the repo root (docker/Dockerfile). Keep it lean and never ship secrets or
# prebuilt outputs - the image rebuilds everything from source.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dist-installer
packages/server/console-dist
packages/server/console-dist.bak-*
packages/server/agent-installer
**/.env
**/.env.local
.git
**/*.log
.state
**/.state
# Windows C++ driver build outputs (not part of the server image)
native-dlp/bin
native-dlp/**/x64
native-dlp/**/Debug
native-dlp/**/Release
# Large repo odds and ends not needed to build the server image
qa
QurantineDats
docs
*.zip
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
# Never ship keys, certificates or release outputs into the build context (and so possibly an
# image layer). docker/extra-ca/*.crt are public CA certificates the build deliberately trusts.
*.key
**/*.key
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.pfx
**/*.pfx
*.p12
**/*.p12
*.crt
**/*.crt
!docker/extra-ca/*.crt
garnet.*
**/garnet.*
certs
**/certs
release
**/release
